      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think matching any specific version is that important, I mostly just need a version of llvm-dev available that meets the minimum (15) so that I can build the Mesa targets instrumented for fuzzing (I guess until we invetiably find an issue that is related to how Mesa interfaces/uses with llvm)\n\nThe technical side of adding to infra/3pp seems reasonably tractable, but reading through the documentation it feels like the process/bueacracy side is pretty heavy weight, with a lot of discussion of taking ownership of the dependency, etc, that I honestly really don\u0027t want to do (i.e. be responsible for rolling some aspect of llvm), or I guess more correctly feels incorrectly scoped to what I am trying to do here, which is enable using our existing infrastructure (CF) for fuzzing this experiment.\n\nSince we already build/package large parts of clang/llvm already I am going to reach out to the people that are OWNERS of that directly and see what advice/direction that they can give, since I feel like I might be going to the wrong way about this.",
